  "security_implications": "event_rx_overflow and event_rx_break_err are combinational event flags that may drive interrupts or status registers; glitches on their inputs (rx_fifo_wvalid/wready, break_err, break_st_q) could cause spurious events, potentially misleading software into false overflow/break-handling actions. The unused_reg signal computes parity of reg2hw.alert_test but is not connected—if alert_test is intended to trigger security alerts, this float may mask incomplete integration and silently suppress alert propagation, though synthesis will usually optimize it away.",
